      "writtenOn": "2022-08-08T14:05:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The current implementation cannot be easily converted to Bazel, because Starlark rules cannot do I/O, and therefore cannot obtain and set the sha256 hash fragment in the output path of these libs while statically constructing the staging directory [1] and the canned_fs_config [2]. \n\n+1 to Jiyong that doing these in apexer (or a different host tool/script) would make transition to Starlark simpler. One way is to make this a two step process: first construct the apex as usual, then if it\u0027s an apex depending on DCLA, then apply a second host tool on the apex and the canned_fs_config to move things around and modify entries.\n\n[1]: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:build/bazel/rules/apex/apex.bzl;l\u003d40;drc\u003d8fac2a129104edd0163ce4fb280833df3c30e1bf\n[2]: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:build/bazel/rules/apex/apex.bzl;l\u003d178;drc\u003d8fac2a129104edd0163ce4fb280833df3c30e1bf",
      "parentUuid": "57b7cf4a_7ba58503",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 423,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 423,
        "endChar": 91
      },
      "revId": "fb975e6fa07731b7bbdfca1d636100b866e45872",
